<title>NEW ZEALAND: Kiwi Income lifts yr profit to NZ$21.0 mln.</title>
<headline>Kiwi Income lifts yr profit to NZ$21.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    21.0 vs 16.1</p>
<p>    Div (cents)			    4.2 vs 3.7</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 7.89 vs 7.80</p>
<p>    Turnover				    39.4 vs 29.96</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			     28.9 vs 21.1</p>
<p>    Tax					    6.5 vs 4.7</p>
<p>    Minorities debit			   1.4 vs 0.3</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	 301.3 vs 241 million</p>
<p>Note - Kiwi Income Property Trust is a property investor.</p>
<p>It said it had net unrealised revaluation gains based on independent valuation of $7.5 million.</p>
<p>It said the fully imputed dividend bought the total return to unitholders to 10.12 cents per unit before tax.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
